.TH THUNDERBIRD-CLOSETOBACKGROUND-DOCTOR 1 "2026-10-24" "Close to Background" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thunderbird-closetobackground-doctor \- check the Thunderbird tray helper and desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thunderbird-closetobackground-doctor
.RB [ --installation-only ]
.RB [ --user-home " directory" ]
.RB [ --system-root " directory" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks native messaging registration, the executable, automatic add-on policy, Python GI bindings, and
the active StatusNotifier tray host. Does not change desktop or Thunderbird settings.
A per-user native manifest takes precedence over the Debian system manifest.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --installation-only
Check the installed files without connecting to the desktop session bus.
.TP
.B --user-home directory
Check a different user directory. The default is the current user's home.
.TP
.B --system-root directory
Inspect an extracted Debian package beneath a staging root. The default is /.
Paths inside its manifest are interpreted relative to that root for this check.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means all requested checks passed. 1 means a check failed.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/thunderbird-closetobackground/thunderbird-closetobackground.xpi
.br
Thunderbird automatically installs or updates this file on its next start
using the policy configured by the Debian package.
.PP
.I /etc/thunderbird/policies/policies.json
.br
System policy, unless an existing application distribution policy was used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thunderbird (1),
.BR dpkg (1)
.PP
/usr/share/doc/thunderbird-closetobackground/README.Debian
